(3 | Proposed Articles of Association) Tj
T*
(To be voted on and signed at the founding meeting. An unincorporated-association organizing instrument, not Articles of) Tj
T*
(Incorporation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 1. Name) Tj
T*
(The name of this association shall be "Chico Homeless Union" \(the "Union"\), subject to name review and adoption) Tj
T*
(by the founding members.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 2. Formation and location) Tj
T*
(The Union is organized by agreement of its founding members as a California nonprofit unincorporated) Tj
T*
(association, headquartered for organizational purposes in Chico, Butte County, California. Date of formation:) Tj
T*
(_______________________.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 3. Nonprofit purpose) Tj
T*
(The Union is organized not for private profit, but for civic, educational, mutual-support, civil-rights, housing, and) Tj
T*
(community-welfare purposes. Its central purpose is to ensure that people currently experiencing homelessness) Tj
T*
(and people with lived experience can organize, represent themselves, seek dignified treatment, and participate in) Tj
T*
(decisions affecting their housing, safety, and rights.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 4. Initial program and advocacy goals) Tj
T*
(Members may pursue changes to Chico camping and public-nuisance ordinances; creation of a Housing and) Tj
T*
(Homelessness Commission; and a lawful, resident-informed proposal for an independent community operator of) Tj
T*
(the Genesis Pallet Shelter. Specific policy demands remain subject to member ratification and amendment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 5. Membership and governance) Tj
T*
(Voting and supporting membership, meetings, elections, leadership duties, finances, and amendments shall be) Tj
T*
(governed by bylaws adopted by the members. People directly affected by homelessness shall retain meaningful) Tj
T*
(democratic control. Membership shall not require payment or a fixed residence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 6. Independence) Tj
T*
(The Union shall not be owned or governed by the City of Chico, the Jesus Center, a shelter contractor, a political) Tj
T*
(party, or any one donor. It may collaborate with organizations while retaining independent decisions. Any) Tj
T*
(national affiliation requires member approval and the national organization's acceptance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 7. Finances and private benefit) Tj
T*
(Any money or property shall be held for authorized nonprofit purposes, documented in financial records, and not) Tj
T*
(distributed to officers or members as private profit. Reasonable reimbursement or compensation for approved) Tj
T*
(work is permitted where lawful and consistent with adopted conflict-of-interest procedures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 8. Dissolution) Tj
T*
(After payment of lawful liabilities, remaining assets shall be distributed for nonprofit public-benefit or social-) Tj
T*
(welfare purposes to one or more qualifying organizations selected by voting members, consistent with then-) Tj
T*
(applicable federal and California law and any tax-exempt status obtained.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Article 9. Adoption) Tj
T*
(These Articles take effect when approved by the founding members at a duly recorded organizational meeting and) Tj
T*
(signed by authorized founding members.) Tj
T*
