(4 | Proposed Bylaws of the Chico Homeless Union) Tj
T*
(Working draft for an unincorporated association. Review with members and counsel before adoption or incorporation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 1. Purpose and authority) Tj
T*
(1.1 The Union advances its purpose in the Articles of Association through lawful collective action, public education,) Tj
T*
(policy participation, mutual support, and accountability work. 1.2 Authority originates with the voting) Tj
T*
(membership. No officer may bind members to a position contrary to an adopted vote.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 2. Membership) Tj
T*
(2.1 Voting membership is open to persons age 18 or older who currently experience homelessness in Chico/Butte) Tj
T*
(County or have experienced homelessness, support the Union's purpose, and affirm membership. Members need) Tj
T*
(not disclose an address, service history, medical condition, or legal history; lived experience is self-attested. No) Tj
T*
(dues are required. 2.2 Supporting membership is open to others who support the purpose; supporting members) Tj
T*
(may volunteer and speak but do not vote on governance, platform, or leadership. 2.3 Every voting member has one) Tj
T*
(vote. 2.4 The Secretary maintains a minimal confidential membership register containing only the name or) Tj
T*
(member-selected identifier, membership class, safe contact method if any, start date, and opt-in communication) Tj
T*
(preferences. 2.5 A member may resign at any time. No person may be expelled without written reasons, a) Tj
T*
(meaningful opportunity to respond, and a two-thirds vote of voting members at a noticed meeting. There shall be) Tj
T*
(no discipline for lawful disagreement, lack of housing, sobriety status, or use of voluntary services.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 3. Meetings, notice, quorum and voting) Tj
T*
(3.1 The Union will hold at least one regular membership meeting monthly at accessible times and locations, with) Tj
T*
(phone or remote participation whenever feasible. 3.2 Notice shall be provided at least seven calendar days in) Tj
T*
(advance by at least two accessible methods, except emergency meetings, for which 48 hours' reasonable notice and) Tj
T*
(a narrowly defined agenda are required. 3.3 Ordinary quorum is the lesser of \(a\) one-third of the current voting) Tj
T*
(membership or \(b\) 10 voting members, but not fewer than three voting members. During formation, until 10) Tj
T*
(voting members are enrolled, quorum is three. 3.4 Ordinary decisions pass by a simple majority of votes cast,) Tj
T*
(excluding abstentions, unless otherwise stated. No proxy votes; members may attend remotely. 3.5 At least seven) Tj
T*
(days' notice must specify any proposed amendment, election, removal, affiliation, incorporation, major financial) Tj
T*
(commitment, or dissolution vote. 3.6 Minutes will record motions and outcomes, not sensitive personal histories.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 4. Leadership) Tj
T*
(4.1 Voting members shall elect a Coordinating Council of five persons, with at least three people currently) Tj
T*
(experiencing homelessness or who experienced homelessness within the preceding five years, subject to their) Tj
T*
(voluntary self-attestation. Until five are available, the founding meeting may elect three interim officers for no) Tj
T*
(more than 120 days. 4.2 Offices: Coordinator, Secretary, Treasurer, and up to two At-Large Representatives. 4.3) Tj
T*
(Terms are one year; members may stand for reelection. 4.4 The Council coordinates authorized work, reports to) Tj
T*
(members, and may not override membership policy votes. 4.5 Any officer can be recalled by a two-thirds vote at a) Tj
T*
(properly noticed meeting with opportunity to respond. Interim vacancies are filled by member vote at the next) Tj
T*
(regular meeting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 5. Meetings of leadership) Tj
T*
(5.1 The Coordinating Council may meet between membership meetings to carry out approved tasks. A majority of) Tj
T*
(filled Council positions constitutes its quorum. 5.2 Leadership must report decisions and expenses at the next) Tj
T*
(membership meeting. 5.3 At least one member directly affected by current homelessness should participate in) Tj
T*
(each significant decision when reasonably possible; if not possible, defer nonurgent policy decisions to the) Tj
T*
(membership.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
