(Section 6. Elections and representation) Tj
T*
(6.1 The Secretary announces nominations at least 14 days before scheduled elections when possible. 6.2 Members) Tj
T*
(may nominate themselves; no proof of permanent address or ID is required, though the Union may maintain) Tj
T*
(reliable membership verification without collecting sensitive documents. 6.3 Contested offices are decided by) Tj
T*
(secret ballot in person or a secure accessible alternative; ties result in a runoff. 6.4 Only authorized spokespersons) Tj
T*
(may communicate official Union decisions. Any member may speak for themselves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 7. Money, contracts and records) Tj
T*
(7.1 No dues are required. Any dues proposal requires a two-thirds membership vote and must preserve free voting) Tj
T*
(membership for people who cannot pay. 7.2 The Treasurer maintains a ledger and receipts. Two authorized) Tj
T*
(approvals are required for payments above $250. 7.3 No person may personally hold Union donations or sign a) Tj
T*
(contract without membership authorization and an appropriate legal/account arrangement. 7.4 Financial reports) Tj
T*
(are presented quarterly and at each annual membership meeting. 7.5 Any contract, funding, or proposed shelter) Tj
T*
(operation must be reviewed for conflicts and member approval before commitment. 7.6 The Union shall not solicit) Tj
T*
(tax-deductible donations unless it has a legally supportable basis to do so.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 8. Conflicts, confidentiality and safety) Tj
T*
(8.1 Officers and members disclose material conflicts involving the City, Genesis, the Jesus Center, contracted) Tj
T*
(providers, or paid consulting. Those affected shall not vote on decisions presenting personal financial conflict. 8.2) Tj
T*
(The Union does not publish members' names, shelter locations, health information, or legal matters without) Tj
T*
(specific informed permission. 8.3 Harassment, threats, retaliation, discrimination, and coercion are prohibited.) Tj
T*
(Meetings should provide accessibility accommodations and respectful participation. 8.4 No one is required to tell a) Tj
T*
(traumatic personal story to participate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 9. Committees and organizing) Tj
T*
(9.1 The Union may create policy, legal information, housing, Genesis oversight, outreach, and mutual-support) Tj
T*
(committees. 9.2 Committees have no authority to sign contracts, handle confidential cases, or make official legal) Tj
T*
(claims without member-approved protocols. 9.3 The Union may obtain independent legal advice and support civil-) Tj
T*
(rights claims; legal standing and representation depend on applicable law and case-specific facts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 10. Legal status and affiliations) Tj
T*
(10.1 Incorporation, any IRS exemption election, and affiliation with the National Union of the Homeless must be) Tj
T*
(approved by two-thirds of votes cast at a noticed membership meeting. 10.2 Any required bylaws amendments for) Tj
T*
(incorporation, IRS qualification, or affiliation shall return to members for approval. 10.3 The Union does not) Tj
T*
(present itself as a National Union chapter until written confirmation is received.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 11. Amendments and dissolution) Tj
T*
(11.1 Bylaw amendments require at least seven days' written or accessible notice of the exact change and approval) Tj
T*
(by two-thirds of votes cast at a quorum meeting. 11.2 Dissolution requires 30 days' notice, an accounting of assets,) Tj
T*
(and approval by three-fourths of votes cast at a quorum meeting. Distribution of remaining assets must comply) Tj
T*
(with the Articles and governing law.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
