(5 | Proposed founding platform) Tj
T*
(For membership deliberation and ratification; policy positions are demands, not current law or existing agreements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Demand 1 | End penalties for unavoidable sheltering) Tj
T*
(The Union is being organized in response to the threat of citations, prosecution, or incarceration of people) Tj
T*
(experiencing homelessness for sleeping or sheltering in public when they have nowhere safe and available to go.) Tj
T*
(Members demand that Chico preserve or adopt explicit ordinance protection against penalizing unavoidable) Tj
T*
(outdoor sleeping or sheltering where no safe, accessible, actually available alternative exists. The Union also seeks) Tj
T*
(safeguards for notice, property, due process, and nonpunitive responses.) Tj
T*
(Suggested public language: "No person should face incarceration simply because they have nowhere else to sleep.) Tj
T*
(Housing is the problem ... homelessness is the outcome.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Demand 2 | Housing and Homelessness Commission) Tj
T*
(The Union demands a permanent City of Chico Commission on Housing and Homelessness, comparable in civic) Tj
T*
(importance to existing commissions for parks, arts, and the airport. Its membership should include people) Tj
T*
(currently experiencing homelessness, people with lived experience, affordable-housing professionals, and) Tj
T*
(community partners. It should publicly review housing production, service access, program outcomes, public) Tj
T*
(contracts, and spending, and report recommendations to the Council.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Demand 3 | Independent community operation of Genesis) Tj
T*
(The Union demands a lawful evaluation and transition pathway for moving day-to-day Genesis Pallet Shelter) Tj
T*
(operations from the Jesus Center to an independent, community-governed operator, with residents and people) Tj
T*
(experiencing homelessness directly involved in decisions, oversight, and service design. The operating) Tj
T*
(organization should provide professional staffing and safe facilities; low-barrier entry; voluntary treatment;) Tj
T*
(transparent budgets and grievance procedures; and pathways to permanent housing. It must be capable of) Tj
T*
(meeting contractual, safety, employment, and funding requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Important distinction concerning Genesis rules) Tj
T*
(The Union seeks to prevent sobriety and mandatory-treatment prerequisites. Earlier Warren settlement conditions) Tj
T*
(already prohibited requiring sobriety to enter or stay at Genesis; this should not be represented as proof that the) Tj
T*
(current operator currently imposes a sobriety entrance requirement. Onsite restrictions on consumption and) Tj
T*
(behavior are separate from requiring sobriety. Review current written rules, resident accounts, and proposed post-) Tj
T*
(settlement changes before making specific compliance claims.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Independent union and separate shelter operator) Tj
T*
(The Union remains a membership organization and watchdog. Any future Genesis operating nonprofit should be a) Tj
T*
(separate, accountable organization to avoid conflicts from the Union both managing a shelter and independently) Tj
T*
(representing its residents. Transfer would require City action and contract review; no transfer is assumed or) Tj
T*
(promised.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
